From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Mon, 07 Sep 2026 20:53:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: emc2305: add DT fan control with minimum PWM duty

Register enabled fan child nodes as independent thermal cooling devices.
Use the hardware PWM byte directly as the cooling state (0..255), and
consume the board's frequency, polarity and output configuration.

Enforce each fan's microchip,pwm-min floor on every thermal and hwmon
request, including zero. Preserve higher boot duty and raise lower duty
before exposing the control interfaces. Hwmon writes set an additional
minimum; clearing it restores thermal demand subject to the board floor.
Serialize control requests and update cached state only after successful
writes. Use managed cooling registration to handle probe failures.

Select direct PWM mode and the 500 RPM tachometer range, deriving RPM
from the configured range. Preserve the controller's hardware spin-up
configuration. Startup needs no software timer or delayed work.

Add the upstream EMC2305 binding with a local minimum-duty property and
KUnit coverage using a simulated SMBus adapter. Exercise all PWM values,
independent floors, manual minimum release, write failures, boot takeover
and tachometer range conversion.

Based on Linux v6.12.103. The base binding is also carried by U-Boot
v2025.10 in dts/upstream/Bindings/hwmon/. Driver changes and the minimum-
duty property are local implementations.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
